    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-1",
      "sourceStart": 1587,
      "sourceEnd": 1677,
      "original": "### 2.1. The span of a list is the smallest subspace containing every vector in that list.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch02-block-0009",
      "sourceStart": 1677,
      "sourceEnd": 1679,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-2",
      "sourceStart": 1679,
      "sourceEnd": 1798,
      "original": "### 2.2. Suppose $v_1,\\ldots,v_m$ is a linearly dependent list in $V$. Then there exists $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ such that",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch02-block-0010",
      "sourceStart": 1798,
      "sourceEnd": 2048,
      "sha256": "a9780a0d9eb1d2d310ec5ac7b1ceda2e129975bce86b99717b60e969d501c0bf"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-3",
      "sourceStart": 2048,
      "sourceEnd": 2173,
      "original": "### 2.3. In the same vector space, the length of a linearly independent list is at most the length of a finite spanning list.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch02-block-0011",
      "sourceStart": 2173,
      "sourceEnd": 2280,
      "sha256": "bdcdfdfd9ea7cd363ffeb8bc5f0a4223289a33c8a7f1a114836318785e8ba2a8"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-4",
      "sourceStart": 2280,
      "sourceEnd": 2408,
      "original": "### 2.4. A list $v_1,\\ldots,v_n$ of vectors in $V$ is a basis if and only if every $v \\in V$ can be written uniquely in the form",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch02-block-0012",
      "sourceStart": 2408,
      "sourceEnd": 2471,
      "sha256": "3b663bdf92e872fa9055034e191da22d0f224ee739f42dddcc6a349f5a390ef5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-5",
      "sourceStart": 2471,
      "sourceEnd": 2530,
      "original": "### 2.5. Every finite-dimensional vector space has a basis.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch02-block-0013",
      "sourceStart": 2530,
      "sourceEnd": 2625,
      "sha256": "7a7ebdb5abc20ccfeb31529296b4e5b047718793c66618a810926f2220b226c7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-6",
      "sourceStart": 2625,
      "sourceEnd": 2729,
      "original": "### 2.6. Every linearly independent set can be extended to a basis of a finite-dimensional vector space.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch02-block-0014",
      "sourceStart": 2729,
      "sourceEnd": 2731,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-7",
      "sourceStart": 2731,
      "sourceEnd": 2841,
      "original": "### 2.7. For every subspace $U$ of a finite-dimensional $V$, there is a subspace $W$ such that $U \\oplus W=V$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch02-block-0015",
      "sourceStart": 2841,
      "sourceEnd": 2843,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-8",
      "sourceStart": 2843,
      "sourceEnd": 2936,
      "original": "### 2.8. The length of any basis of a finite-dimensional vector space $V$ is always the same.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch02-block-0016",
      "sourceStart": 2936,
      "sourceEnd": 3202,
      "sha256": "45968ffa492a7d0f00e7b420e373b1b5b9f78d60b134a02e6433e90d03aa0996"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch02-item-2-9",
      "sourceStart": 3202,
      "sourceEnd": 3286,
      "original": "### 2.9. If $V_1$ and $V_2$ are subspaces of a finite-dimensional vector space, then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
